      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/xiphophorus-signum-4/",
      "html": "<p>This species of swordtail is only very rarely offered in the trade. At first glimpse one may think they are a variety of the common swordtail X. hellerii, but X. signum is much more slender.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/xiphophorus-signum-4/",
      "html": "<p>Xiphophorus signum is, like most wild types of swordtail, quite demanding. It needs clear, bacteria-poor water.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/xiphophorus-signum-4/",
      "html": "<p>It needs proper feeding with different types of food, including frozen and live food.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/xiphophorus-signum-4/",
      "html": "<p>The mark responsible for the scientific name (Latin signum = sign) is always clearly visible in females on the caudal fin base, while in males it is covered by the dark border of the sword.</p>"
    }
  ],
